== missing
file: .github/workflows/extra.yml
message: has no top-level permissions, so it gets the repository's default, which may be write
fix: set top-level `permissions: contents: read` (or `read-all`, or `{}`) and grant write scopes in the job that needs them

== a write scope
file: .github/workflows/extra.yml
message: line 3: top-level permissions grant security-events: write
fix: move security-events: write into the permissions of the job that needs it; keep top-level scopes read or none

== write-all
file: .github/workflows/extra.yml
message: line 2: top-level permissions are write-all, not read-all
fix: set top-level `permissions: contents: read` (or `read-all`, or `{}`) and grant write scopes in the job that needs them

